-- title:
--   Transcendental residue forces value group of 𝒪 to equal that of A
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A$ a valuation subring of $L$, with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and residue map $\mathrm{residue}_A : A \to k$. Let $F$ be a field equipped with an $L$-algebra structure and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a valuation subring of $F$ such that, for every $x \in L$, the image of $x$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal{O}$ if and only if $x \in A$ (so $\mathcal{O}$ contracts to $A$ on $L$). Let $\bar F$ be a field which is a $k$-algebra, and let $\rho : \mathcal{O} \to \bar F$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal{O}$ and which is compatible with the residue map on $A$, in the sense that for every $a \in A$ one has $\rho(a) = \mathrm{residue}_A(a)$ viewed in $\bar F$ via the $k$-algebra structure. Assume some $f \in \mathcal{O}$ has $\rho(f)$ transcendental over $k$, and that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field $L(f) = L(\{f\})$ generated by $f$. Then for every $h \in F$ with $h \neq 0$ there exists $c \in L$ with $c \cdot h \in \mathcal{O}$ and $\rho(c \cdot h) \neq 0$, i.e. $c\,h$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   This is the regularity (ramification index one) statement for a prolongation $\mathcal{O}$ of a valuation $A$ of the constant field to a function field $F$ of transcendence degree one over $L$: the hypothesis that some element of $\mathcal{O}$ has transcendental residue identifies the value group of $\mathcal{O}$ with that of $A$, since every nonzero $h \in F$ becomes a unit after multiplication by a constant. It is used in the construction of regular prolongations for algebraic curves, via [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_of_forall_mem_adjoin_iff_of_isAlgebraic`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_of_forall_mem_adjoin_iff_of_isAlgebraic).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_smul_mem_of_transcendental_residue.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ValuationSubring.exists_smul_mem_of_transcendental_residue
    {L : Type*} [Field L] [IsAlgClosed L] (A : ValuationSubring L)
    {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra L F]
    (O : ValuationSubring F) (hO : ∀ x : L, algebraMap L F x ∈ O ↔ x ∈ A)
    {Fbar : Type*} [Field Fbar] [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) Fbar]
    (ρ : O →+* Fbar) (hker : RingHom.ker ρ = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O)
    (hρ : ∀ a : A, ρ ⟨algebraMap L F a, (hO a).mpr a.2⟩ =
      algebraMap (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) Fbar (IsLocalRing.residue A a))
    (f : F) (hf : f ∈ O)
    (htr : Transcendental (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) (ρ ⟨f, hf⟩))
    [Algebra.IsAlgebraic (IntermediateField.adjoin L ({f} : Set F)) F]
    (h : F) (hh : h ≠ 0) :
    ∃ c : L, ∃ hc : c • h ∈ O, ρ ⟨c • h, hc⟩ ≠ 0 := by sorry
